    {
      "title": "Roles in the harbour",
      "note": "in force, defined in the glossary",
      "status": "in force",
      "line": 21,
      "lines": [
        {
          "line": 23,
          "last": 24,
          "text": "- **pilot**: the session at the harbour's main pier, with the captain: answers, writes cargo notes, does all the work in a small harbour and only assists once the harbour has a skipper (the captain, 2031-01-05: \"1a\").",
          "bullet": true
        },
        {
          "line": 25,
          "last": 25,
          "text": "- **skipper**: runs one ship and hands out routes.",
          "bullet": true
        },
        {
          "line": 26,
          "last": 27,
          "text": "- **deckhand**: a helper inside a session (no berth of its own); in force since the captain used it (2031-01-05: \"the running skippers, deckhands\"). German words: open.",
          "bullet": true
        },
        {
          "line": 28,
          "last": 28,
          "text": "- a fourth role without a name yet (\"mate\", \"bosun\" proposed).",
          "bullet": true
        }
      ],
      "tables": []
    },
